    1 000000             ! ============================================================
    2 000000             ! PRINTER85 v0.03b RC1b -- HP-85 OPTION ROM
    3 000000             !
    4 000000             ! v0.03b RC1b is an assembler-corrected architectural refactor of the hardware-verified v0.03a
    5 000000             ! RC1a common text/key-panel build.  It introduces a table-driven printer
    6 000000             ! driver interface so printer-specific control sequences and behavior can be
    7 000000             ! added as self-contained driver blocks without changing the PRINTER85 core.
    8 000000             !
    9 000000             ! Public behavior is intended to remain unchanged from v0.03a RC1a.
   10 000000             !
   11 000000             ! RC1a fixed the 22 CAPASM parser errors in RC1.  RC1b additionally avoids the
   12 000000             ! one remaining out-of-range relative JMP in DRVKEY by calling DRVGO with a
   13 000000             ! literal-direct JSB and then returning normally.
   14 000000             !
   15 000000             ! CAPASM accepts a
   16 000000             ! multi-byte immediate such as ADM R34,=2,0, but does not accept an
   17 000000             ! EQU symbol as the first element of that comma-separated literal
   18 000000             ! (for example ADM R34,=DMAXZ,0).  Descriptor offsets therefore use
   19 000000             ! their explicit octal ABI values in ADM instructions, with the
   20 000000             ! symbolic field name retained in the comment.  No driver behavior
   21 000000             ! or descriptor layout is changed.
   22 000000             !
   23 000000             ! Baseline Option-ROM build derived from the hardware-verified PRINTER85
   24 000000             ! v0.01a standalone LOADBIN implementation and the v0.02a Option-ROM port.
   25 000000             !
   26 000000             ! v0.02b fixes two Option-ROM-specific issues established by hardware tests:
   27 000000             !
   28 000000             !   1. COPY/PAPER handled-key exit:
   29 000000             !      KHOOK returns normally through ROMJSB and a RAM trampoline performs
   30 000000             !      the documented R6 handled-key exit only after ROMJSB has unwound.
   31 000000             !
   32 000000             !   2. SII graphics hardcopy:
   33 000000             !      Use CRTWPO/CRTUNW for fast CRT reads without powering the CRT down.
   34 000000             !      Caller wipeout state is preserved; PRINTER85 unwipes only if it wiped.
   35 000000             !      Both routines are documented ROMJSB=N and are safe direct calls from
   36 000000             !      an external ROM.
   37 000000             !
   38 000000             ! The v0.02d RC3 SII page-mode reliability sequence is retained unchanged:
   39 000000             ! ESC S -> wait -> ESC J 0 -> wait -> ESC L -> wait -> page setup/raster -> FF.
   40 000000             ! The proven CRTWPO/CRTUNW and RAM-trampoline architecture is also retained.
   41 000000             !
   42 000000             ! ThinkJet support in PRINTER85 deliberately assumes HP control-sequence mode
   43 000000             ! (switch 5 DOWN).  Alternate/Epson-emulation mode is outside project scope.
   44 000000             !
   45 000000             ! Existing raster formatting and hardcopy behavior are otherwise unchanged.
   46 000000             !
   47 000000             ! ROM number: 0241 octal
   48 000000             ! ROM base:   060000 octal
   49 000000             ! ROM complement byte: 0136 octal (0241 + 0136 = 0377)
   50 000000             !
   51 000000             ! Public keywords:
   52 000000             !
   53 000000             !       PVER
   54 000000             !       PRTSCREEN device,driver[,zoom[,orientation]]
   55 000000             !       PRTSET    device,driver[,zoom[,orientation]]
   56 000000             !       PRTKEYS   mode
   57 000000             !       PRTPITCH  pitch
   58 000000             !       PRTLPI    lines_per_inch
   59 000000             !       PRTBOLD   mode
   60 000000             !       PRTUNDER  mode
   61 000000             !       PRTNORM
   62 000000             !       PRTZOOM   zoom
   63 000000             !       PRTORIENT orientation
Page    1                                                             
CAPASM

   64 000000             !
   65 000000             ! v0.03a introduced the first common text/control utility layer for both
   66 000000             ! ThinkJet and SII printers, plus a native HP-85 K1..K8 control panel:
   67 000000             !
   68 000000             !       K1 pitch        K5 line spacing
   69 000000             !       K2 bold         K6 underline
   70 000000             !       K3 COPY zoom    K7 COPY orientation
   71 000000             !       K4 previous     K8 next page
   72 000000             !
   73 000000             ! v0.03b RC1a still exposes only the COMMON key page for the built-in drivers.
   74 000000             ! KEY LABEL buffers are saved/restored by PRTKEYS 1/0.  Labels are rendered
   75 000000             ! as seven visible characters plus one separating blank per 8-byte slot.
   76 000000             !
   77 000000             ! Driver 1 = HP ThinkJet 2225A
   78 000000             ! Driver 2 = SII IFD501 / CAPD345A
   79 000000             !
   80 000000             ! Driver architecture (v0.03b):
   81 000000             !   - DRVTAB is the only registry of installed printer personalities.
   82 000000             !   - each descriptor supplies capability bytes plus routine pointers for
   83 000000             !     pitch/LPI/bold/underline, paper controls, text/graphics close policy,
   84 000000             !     graphics hardcopy, and future private K-key pages;
   85 000000             !   - the core dispatches through descriptor pointers with indexed JSB;
   86 000000             !   - adding a driver normally means copying the template block near DRVTAB,
   87 000000             !     filling its routines/sequences, then adding one DEF to DRVTAB and
   88 000000             !     incrementing DRVNUM.
   89 000000             !
   90 000000             ! ROM/RAM architecture:
   91 000000             !   - all executable code and immutable tables live in ROM 0241;
   92 000000             !   - 01600 octal (896 decimal) bytes are permanently reserved at power-on;
   93 000000             !   - BAS241 (102554 octal) holds the base address of that writable workspace;
   94 000000             !   - all former LOADBIN BSZ state/buffers are offsets in that RAM workspace;
   95 000000             !   - CHIDLE is still opt-in via PRTKEYS 1;
   96 000000             !   - a RAM trampoline lets ROMJSB unwind before the handled-key R6 exit is
   97 000000             !     performed.  CHIDLE contains JSB <RAM trampoline> / RTN.
   98 000000             !   - the RAM trampoline calls ROMJSB -> KHOOK in ROM 241, then performs the
   99 000000             !     proven handled-key pop only after ROMJSB has completely returned.
  100 000000             !
  101 000000             ! Important: PRTKEYS is NOT installed automatically at power-on or RESET.
  102 000000             ! ============================================================
  103 000000             
  104 000000                     ABS ROM 60000
