 3710 072402             
 3711 072402             ! ============================================================
 3712 072402             ! SII DRIVER 2 -- v0.02d RC3 PAGE MODE / RELIABLE ENTRY
 3713 072402             !
 3714 072402             ! Target hardware:
 3715 072402             !       Seiko Instruments IFD501-01UK-E
 3716 072402             !       CAPD345A 576-dot thermal mechanism
 3717 072402             !
 3718 072402             ! Page-mode sequence used here:
 3719 072402             !
 3720 072402             !       ESC S                       force/cancel any residual page mode
 3721 072402             !       [settling delay]
 3722 072402             !       ESC J 0                     flush standard line buffer, zero feed
 3723 072402             !       [settling delay]
 3724 072402             !       ESC L                       enter page mode from known line start
 3725 072402             !       [settling delay]
 3726 072402             !       ESC W x y dx dy             define exact image print area
 3727 072402             !       ESC T 0                     top-left, left-to-right
 3728 072402             !       ESC $ 0 0                   horizontal deployment position = 0
 3729 072402             !       GS  $ 0 0                   vertical deployment position = 0
 3730 072402             !       GS v 0 ...                  ONE complete raster image command
 3731 072402             !       [payload streamed in chunks]
 3732 072402             !       FF                          batch print + return to standard mode
 3733 072402             !
 3734 072402             ! RC3 addresses the intermittent failure where GS v 0 payload bytes were
 3735 072402             ! visibly printed as structured text.  ESC L is documented as valid only at
 3736 072402             ! the beginning of a line.  The conservative ESC S / ESC J 0 / ESC L preamble
 3737 072402             ! establishes standard mode and a clean line start before page-mode selection.
 3738 072402             ! ESC J 0 has zero feed distance; if residual line data exists it flushes one
 3739 072402             ! line and leaves the next position at the beginning of a line.
 3740 072402             !
 3741 072402             ! The IFD501 manual recommends explicitly establishing a deployment position
 3742 072402             ! after entering page mode / setting the print area.  ESC $ and GS $ do that;
Page   66                                                             
CAPASM

 3743 072402             ! no LF or ESC 3 line-spacing commands are used inside page mode.
 3744 072402             !
 3745 072402             ! Important: the GS v 0 raster is deliberately one logical image, not a set of
 3746 072402             ! eight-row images.  HPOUT transaction boundaries do not add printer data.  The
 3747 072402             ! physically-proven v0.10h SII driver already streamed one GS v 0 header followed
 3748 072402             ! by many independent HPOUT payload chunks, so this preserves that proven parser
 3749 072402             ! behaviour while page mode absorbs the entire image before the final FF.
 3750 072402             !
 3751 072402             ! Default IFD501 basic calculation pitch is x=y=203, i.e. one CAPD345 dot.
 3752 072402             ! ESC W therefore uses physical output dimensions in dots:
 3753 072402             !
 3754 072402             !       portrait  z1 : 256 x 192
 3755 072402             !       portrait  z2 : 512 x 384
 3756 072402             !       landscape z1 : 192 x 256
 3757 072402             !       landscape z2 : 384 x 512
 3758 072402             ! ============================================================
 3759 072402             
 3760 072402 230         SIIDRV  BIN
 3761 072403 114 261 154         LDMD R14,=BAS241
      072406 205 
