 3796 072506             ! R46/R47 -> 21-byte page-mode setup table beginning with ESC W.
 3797 072506             ! R32/R33 -> 8-byte full-image GS v 0 header.
 3798 072506             ! Preserve the header pointer across the setup output in SIIDST.
 3799 072506             !
 3800 072506             ! Reliable-entry preamble:
 3801 072506             !   1. ESC S   -- if still in page mode, return to standard mode and discard
 3802 072506             !                 stale page data; ignored when already in standard mode.
 3803 072506             !   2. ESC J 0 -- in standard mode, flush any residual line buffer with zero
 3804 072506             !                 feed distance and leave the next position at line start.
 3805 072506             !   3. ESC L   -- enter page mode from the documented required line-start state.
 3806 072506             !
 3807 072506             ! Each state-changing command is sent as its own HPOUT transaction and followed
 3808 072506             ! by the existing conservative SII settling delay.  The actual GS v 0 header and
 3809 072506             ! payload remain contiguous logically and receive no inserted delays.
 3810 072506             
 3811 072506 132 014 267 SIPGSET STMD R32,X14,SIIDST
      072511 357 001 
